# Studio ship checklist

When adding or changing a user-facing studio feature:

1. Update `src/lib/featureRegistry.js` guidebook copy (and a diagnostic check in `src/lib/diagnosticChecks.js` when the behavior is testable). Prefer extending an existing step; add a new `diagnosticFunction` only when the feature cannot be covered by current checks.
2. Keep HUD step count honest: never hardcode "13단계". Use `DIAG_STEPS.length`.
3. After the code is done, always:
   - `git add .`
   - `git commit` with a concise why-focused message
   - `git tag -a vX.Y.Z-stable-backup -m "... Stable Backup"` (bump patch from the latest `v*-stable-backup` tag)
   - `git push origin main`
   - `git push origin vX.Y.Z-stable-backup`
4. Do not skip tag/push because the change looks small. The user asked for backup + GitHub Pages redeploy on every additional work item.
